Conformance

For purposes of this reference license, an implementation may be considered compatible if it preserves:

structure-based correctness

deterministic truth resolution

certificate reproducibility

deterministic replay behavior

structural truth visibility

equivalent truth under equivalent structure

explicit handling of structural inconsistency

For purposes of this reference license and reference implementation, conformance is evaluated through observable behavior.

`same structure -> same observable truth -> same certificate`

Normalization Requirement

For deterministic certificate identity:

`normalized_truth = normalize(truth)`

`certificate = hash(normalized_truth)`

Normalization ensures:

independence from representation format

consistent identity across systems

consistent replay behavior

SHA-256 is used in the reference implementation for demonstration.

Deterministic Replay Property

Replay explores preservation of the invariant:

`same structure -> same observable truth -> same certificate`

Within the bounded reference model, replay explores preservation of observable truth under identical structural conditions.

This explores:

replay -> same observable truth

Observable truth depends upon structure.

Not replay ordering or replay sequence.

Relationship to Shunyaya Framework

STRUE is part of the broader Shunyaya framework.

It builds upon a broader structural direction exploring dependency elimination and structure-preserved correctness.

Each direction explores removal of assumed dependencies while preserving correctness through structure.

