Closing Statement

STRUE explores a simple but fundamental question:

Observable truth may remain structurally visible.

Maintained current structure may preserve observable truth.

STRUE explores whether traversal-based rediscovery during retrieval is fundamentally required within the bounded reference model.

Traversal may reveal truth.

Structure may preserve observable truth.

STRUE is released to encourage:

independent validation

real-world testing

safe experimentation

STRUE is offered as a minimal, verifiable reference implementation of that possibility.
